">16459043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blanc</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Nahimana</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Petignat</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wenger</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bille</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Francioli</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Faucets as a reservoir of endemic <italic>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</italic> colonization/infections in intensive care units</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1964</fpage><lpage>1968</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00134-004-2389-z</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Blanc&#x000a0;DS, Nahimana&#x000a0;I, Petignat&#x000a0;C, Wenger&#x000a0;A, Bille&#x000a0;J, Francioli&#x000a0;P (2004) Faucets as a&#x000a0;reservoir of endemic Pseudomonas aeruginosa colonization/infections in intensive care units. Intensive Care Med 30:1964&#x02013;1968 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15257431</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schelenz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>French</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An outbreak of multidrug-resistant <italic>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</italic> infection associated with contamination of bronchoscopes and an endoscope washer-disinfector</article-title><source>J Hosp Infect</source><year>2000</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/jhin.2000.0800</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Schelenz&#x000a0;S, French&#x000a0;G (2000) An outbreak of 